{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/199798-serenity-rpg","id":199798,"title":"Serenity RPG","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-17T01:35:36-07:00","id":199798,"title":"Serenity RPG","content":"Just been reading the Serenity RPG (no, not the Firefly RPG. Is it just me, or is it weird both exist, both made more-or-less by the same company, using systems that, while not identical, are very similar?). Has anyone played using it, and have you found any problems? For example, something that seems like it might be an issue is most everything for character creation runs off Attribute points. Fair enough. But your Attributes have to be at least d4, which costs 4 AP. Ok, fair enough again. But what happens if you don't? I mean, I would interpret &quot;attributes have to be at least X&quot; would imply that you <i>start</i> with a rating of X, and buy it up with points, but the examples pretty clearly imply, if not outright state, that you have to buy them up to d4. So, they <i>say</i> you start with e.g. 42 AP, but given that you have 6 Attributes, you really only have 18, which is pretty little to work with to make a whole character with skills, attributes, assets and the like. I suppose complications help there a little, but still. That seems weird to me. Stuff like that.<br /> <br /> Or does it work anyway, and I'm totally wrong. How does it actually play?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T04:29:58-07:00","id":199892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/199798-serenity-rpg#post199798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just been reading the Serenity RPG (no, not the Firefly RPG. Is it just me, or is it weird both exist, both made more-or-less by the same company, using systems that, while not identical, are very similar?).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have both. Serenity is the original game from which the &quot;Cortex&quot; and &quot;Cortex Plus&quot; RPG system originated. Firefly and the other system from Margaret Weiss Productions now use Cortex Plus as their base plateform. A bit like how Chaosium BRP, Call of Cthulhu, etc. are derived from the RuneQuest system. It may sound weird, but it's really a licencing issues. They had the licence for Serenity...then several year nothing, and now they have the licence for Firefly. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/199798-serenity-rpg#post199798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, something that seems like it might be an issue is most everything for character creation runs off Attribute points. Fair enough. <u>But your Attributes have to be <b>at least</b> d4, which costs 4 AP.</u> Ok, fair enough again. But what happens if you don't? I mean, I would interpret &quot;attributes have to be at least X&quot; would imply that you <i>start</i> with a rating of X, and buy it up with points, but the examples pretty clearly imply, if not outright state, that you have to buy them up to d4..</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I don't see any issue here. Your key word here is <u><b>&quot;At least&quot;: </b></u>so it cannot be lower the d4, but can be above d4...otherwise they would have said &quot;it must be at most dX&quot; or &quot;ranging from dX to dY&quot;. So yes, from your total pool you need to invest a minimum of 24 points for your stats (d4 x6)... that your baseline human, but if you want to have a couple stronger stats at d6, or d8, you just pay the diffierence and voil\u00e0.<br /> <br /> The system is meant to encourage player to choose wisely and be good in a couple of skills, but not be uber-human and have amazing skills across the board.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/199798-serenity-rpg#post199798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Or does it work anyway, and I'm totally wrong. How does it actually play?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it plays really well, I once played a game where I had a ex-special ops and it was a really fun game that ran pretty smoothly...we had to stop for various RL issues, but that's a different story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T05:08:27-07:00","id":199899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/199798-serenity-rpg?p=199892#post199892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I don't see any issue here. Your key word here is <u><b>&quot;At least&quot;: </b></u>so it cannot be lower the d4, but can be above d4...otherwise they would have said &quot;it must be at most dX&quot; or &quot;ranging from dX to dY&quot;. So yes, from your total pool you need to invest a minimum of 24 points for your stats (d4 x6)... that your baseline human, but if you want to have a couple stronger stats at d6, or d8, you just pay the diffierence and voil\u00e0.<br /> <br /> The system is meant to encourage player to choose wisely and be good in a couple of skills, but not be uber-human and have amazing skills across the board.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I get that, it just seems with, at least based on how I read it, you'd sort of by necessity end up having to be pretty specialised, which <i>can</i> be a problem for character versatility? Not &quot;I do everything and am awesome&quot; versatility, but things like &quot;Mechanics is my main passion, but I grew up on a rough planet so I can take care of myself in a fistfight, and picked up a smattering of medical knowledge&quot;. You know, those skills you put a few points in not for effectiveness, but because they help establish your character in a way simple backstory can't, at least as easily. (as important as that stuff is). So you'd end up kind of one-note, I would think? Or is it more sort of expected that you won't, initially, be particularly spectacular at anything, i.e. ratings of more than e.g. d6 in a skill are unusual for a starting character?<br /> <br /> There's also the question of why they give you, e.g. 42 points when 24 are spoken for, would think it'd be easier to just say you have 18, and these things start at d4. Same result, just bit less...well, pointless isn't the word, but I can't think of a better one. But that's not really a game-design or play issue, just something I find odd that they did it the way they did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T06:43:42-07:00","id":199960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/199798-serenity-rpg?p=199899#post199899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the question of why they give you, e.g. 42 points when 24 are spoken for, would think it'd be easier to just say you have 18, and these things start at d4. Same result, just bit less...well, pointless isn't the word, but I can't think of a better one. But that's not really a game-design or play issue, just something I find odd that they did it the way they did.</div> </div> </div> </div>To make the math easy. You add up all your attributes, and if you get 42 you're done. Serenity's a lot of fun, though I found the system breaks horribly if you let the players minmax and they start with way too much cash.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T07:10:15-07:00","id":199984,"title":"","content":"I suppose that makes sense. I usually just work on a 'count-down' method when I'm making characters, X points to start, -3 for this, -2 for that, when I hit zero then I'm done. Didn't take into account the need to check, or that other people might do things differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T14:53:06-07:00","id":200419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/199798-serenity-rpg?p=199899#post199899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Or is it more sort of expected that you won't, initially, be particularly spectacular at anything, i.e. ratings of more than e.g. d6 in a skill are unusual for a starting character?.</div> </div> </div> </div>To my experience, pretty much yes. Either that or you are awesome in 1 field, but poor in the rest.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T15:50:39-07:00","id":201533,"title":"","content":"Just to stick my nose in, I got to help with the she